## Talks & Science Communication

**2026 — Archives Henri Poincaré, Strasbourg**

*On the notion of objectivity in astrophysics.*

Presentation exploring the epistemological foundations of objectivity in astrophysical research, focusing on the relationship between observational evidence, theoretical models and the construction of scientific knowledge.

**2025 — Jardin des Sciences, Strasbourg University**

*The history of large-scale structure in the Universe.*

Public outreach conference exploring the historical development of the concept of large-scale structure, from early descriptions of galaxy distributions to the emergence of the cosmic web as a central framework in modern cosmology.
